.TH TRES 1 "November 2026" "Tres 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tres \- minimal three-square Wayland desktop and helper commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tres-session
.br
.B tres-config
.br
.B tres-panel
.br
.B tres-panel-supervisor
.br
.B tres-panel-control restart
.br
.B tres-search
.br
.B tres-screenshot
.br
.B tres-open-files
.br
.B tres-open-terminal
.br
.B tres-wallpaper
.br
.B tres-synaptic
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Tres
is a minimal standalone Wayland desktop session built on Labwc.
Three small squares provide the application launcher, running-window
selection, and system applets without a traditional taskbar.
.PP
Normally, start Tres by choosing
.B Tres
from the display manager's session chooser. The
.B tres-session
command sets up Tres's private Labwc session and starts the compositor.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tres-session
Start the desktop session. Normally called by the display manager.
.TP
.B tres-config
Open Tres configuration for display scaling, positioning, appearance,
keyboard shortcuts, and default applications.
.TP
.B tres-panel
Run the three-square panel within a Wayland session.
.TP
.B tres-panel-supervisor
Start and supervise the panel, restarting it after unexpected exits.
.TP
.B tres-panel-control restart
Restart the currently supervised Tres panel.
.TP
.B tres-search
Open Tres application search.
.TP
.B tres-screenshot
Open the screenshot utility for full-screen and area capture.
.TP
.B tres-open-files
Open the user's home directory with the configured file manager.
.TP
.B tres-open-terminal
Launch the configured terminal emulator.
.TP
.B tres-wallpaper
Launch the configured Tres background using swaybg.
.TP
.B tres-synaptic
Start Synaptic with graphical privilege authorization if Synaptic is installed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tres/
User-controlled Tres settings and state.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tres/labwc/
Labwc autostart, mouse and keyboard bindings, and menu configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/tres/
Session and panel diagnostic logs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR labwc (1),
.BR swaybg (1),
.BR grim (1),
.BR slurp (1)
